SGLang patch on top of the vendored llama.cpp tree (ggml/, see ggml/LLAMA_CPP_COMMIT), applied after
0002-mmq-iq1_m.patch.

MMQ, MUL_MAT_ID: the stream-k fixup skips the tiles past an expert's columns before reading their ids.

mul_mat_q_stream_k_fixup reads ids_dst[col_low + jt*J + j] for j < J in every tile jt of ncols_max and only
then finds the tile empty (j_max < 0). For an expert with fewer columns than the tile index reaches, the
reads run up to (ntx - 1) * J entries past the expert's ids and past the end of ids_dst; nothing read there is
used, so it is harmless while that memory is mapped, and an illegal address (an MMU fault in the fixup) when
ids_dst ends an allocation next to unmapped address space. The main kernel already returns for these tiles
(jt*J >= col_diff); the fixup now does the same. The written values do not change.

--- a/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
+++ b/src/ggml-cuda/mmq.cuh
@@ -1390,6 +1390,12 @@
     const int col_high = expert_bounds[zt + 1];
     const int col_diff = col_high - col_low;
 
+    // A tile past this expert's columns writes nothing (j_max < 0 below); reading its ids ran up
+    // to (ntx - 1) * J entries past ids_dst. The main kernel skips the same tiles (jt*J >= col_diff).
+    if (jt*J >= col_diff) {
+        return;
+    }
+
     for (int j = threadIdx.y*warp_size + threadIdx.x; j < J; j += nwarps*warp_size) {
         ids_dst_shared[j] = ids_dst[col_low + jt*J + j];
     }
